  "worked_solution": "The level curves for the function $f(x,y)$ are given by the equations \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=c.\n$$\n\nNotice that the range of $f(x,y)$ is $[0,\\infty ).$ So, we will consider only $c$-level curves for $c\\ge 0.$\n\nTherefore, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & =c \\\\ \\sqrt{y+2{x}^{2}} & =c \\\\ y+2{x}^{2} & ={c}^{2} \\\\ y & ={c}^{2}-2{x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation above gives us a family of parabolas with the vertex at $(0,{c}^{2}).$ Therefore, the correct graph is as follows:\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14095515/assets/6b425704394d6fcd3090b54a3767b031b728cf4dbc44f9ac9446defe1cdb05aa.png)",
